     "cause": "implementation",
     "answer": "The plan is wrong in two places and must be amended; then Sirius re-runs. (1) In checkDeliverable's label regex, change the lookahead from `(?![\\w])` to `(?![A-Za-z0-9])` so a trailing `_`/`__` emphasis closer is allowed. `Makings` is still refused, because `s` stays excluded. (2) Plan item 7 gives the fake-pi restate detector as `/^Your report was refused at hand-off\\./`, which contradicts the plan's own restatePrompt (`hand-off: it lacks…`) and title 5's assertions. Correct it to `/^Your report was refused at hand-off:/`. Under D9 that one-line edit in test/fake-pi.mjs:24 goes to Orion as part of the plan correction; Sirius must not make it. Keep restatePrompt's colon form as written.",
     "evidence": "test/handoff.test.mjs:53 (`### __Waits on__`) and :55 (`_Waits on_: y`) are emphasis-wrapped labels that the plan's title 1 says must be found ('headings, bold or plain'). The plan's own regex allows a leading `[*_]{1,2}`, but its `(?![\\w])` rejects the closing `_`, so the plan's regex misses its own stated intent. test/fake-pi.mjs:24 is `/^Your report was refused at hand-off\\./`, copied verbatim from plan item 7. Plan item 4 and test/handoff.test.mjs:239, 255 and 263 all use `refused at hand-off: it lacks required parts (…)`, so the restate flag is never true and titles 3, 4, 5 and 8 fail (e.g. :156, :193 count `c.restate`). Both defects come from the plan contradicting itself, not from Sirius's code or from Orion departing from the plan.",
     "by": "Arbiter"
    },
    "prerequisite": null,
    "report": "Sirius (implement) could not do the step as written: Two places where the plan and Orion's tests disagree. I implemented the plan as written, so `handoff.test.mjs` is 4 pass, 5 fail. I made no commits"
   }
